Here are some things that I personally don't like much about Moria:

The levels are too big, something like 9 computer screens per level.
All the scrolling back and forth gets to be annoying, especially
when I'm trying to find a staircase.  The problem is worsened when
I haven't yet found a Word of Recall, and have to trudge through
new unmapped levels on my way up to the town.

The bartering system in Moria is also very much of a pain.  I've often
had to make as many as thirty offers to get the best deal out of any
shop.  If I don't do that, often the markup/down is as much as 300%
(on top of the built-in buy/sell markup)

Then there are those thieves, brigands, etc.  Sure, Nethack has
nymphs and leprechauns which steal from you, but at least they
keep what they stole.  In Moria, anything that is stolen from you
disappears from the face of the earth.  That's a Real problem when
you lose a spellbook and thereby the use of a whole list of your spells.

I'll prefer Nethack any day of the week, even if there's a new moon. :)

